{
  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_013 (image-only, ViT-L, singleprofile) scored 0.227 acc, while config_012 (multimodal, scgpt+ViT-L, weighted, singleprofile) scored 0.422 acc. This ~0.20 gap shows the multimodal combination is strong, but we cannot yet tell how much is driven by the RNA modality versus the image modality or their interaction. Uncertainty: We have no RNA-only baseline, so we don't know whether scgpt alone approaches 0.42 (implying image adds little) or is much lower (implying genuine multimodal synergy). Question tested: config_048 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_012—removing only the image modality while keeping the same RNA encoder (scgpt) and profile setting (singleprofile). Why best next: With only two completed experiments, the highest-information move is to establish each modality's individual contribution before investing in fusion/aggregation/profile variants. The result will sharply redirect the search: if RNA alone ≈ 0.40, we should prioritize RNA encoder choices; if RNA alone ≈ 0.25, multimodal fusion is genuinely synergistic and we should explore aggregation and fusion strategies; if RNA alone is very low, image features are critical and we should test alternative image encoders. No other available configuration isolates this question as cleanly."
}

